---- RATIONALE ----

>> A6: Is your inode structure a multilevel index?  If so, why did you
>> choose this particular combination of direct, indirect, and doubly
>> indirect blocks?  If not, why did you choose an alternative inode
>> structure, and what advantages and disadvantages does your
>> structure have, compared to a multilevel index?

My implementation is multilevel index and the reason that I choose this
is to enable extending the file when another file is located right next
to the file. Previous implementation cannot extend the file in that case,
since it marked its location of the file by length, the file must be located
continuously. However, in this implementation the file do not need be located
continuously, so the file can be extend even though another file located right
next to it.

