>> B5: Does your implementation allow a directory to be removed if it
>> is open by a process or if it is in use as a process's current
>> working directory?  If so, what happens to that process's future
>> file system operations?  If not, how do you prevent it?

When we call inode_remove, it only sets the member of the inode structure
removed as true, and does not remove the inode from the disk.
Also, it removes in the inode_close function only when the inode's open count
become 0 and removed flag is set to true. So inode would not be closed
while it is opened by another thread.

